    37→/**
    38→ * Provides a singleton value of type {@code <T>} from {@code Properties} bound in guice.
    39→ * <br/>
    40→ * <h3>Usage</h3>
    41→ * To install this provider, bind it in your guice module, like below.
    42→ *
    43→ * <pre>
    44→ * JsonConfigProvider.bind(binder, "druid.server", DruidServerConfig.class);
    45→ * </pre>
    46→ * <br/>
    47→ * In the above case, {@code druid.server} should be a key found in the {@code Properties} bound elsewhere.
    48→ * The value of that key should directly relate to the fields in {@code DruidServerConfig.class}.
    49→ *
    50→ * <h3>Implementation</h3>
    51→ * <br/>
    52→ * The state of {@code <T>} is defined by the value of the property {@code propertyBase}.
    53→ * This value is a json structure, decoded via {@link JsonConfigurator#configurate(Properties, String, Class)}.
    54→ * <br/>
    55→ *
    56→ * An example might be if DruidServerConfig.class were
    57→ *
    58→ * <pre>
    59→ *   public class DruidServerConfig
    60→ *   {
    61→ *     @JsonProperty @NotNull public String hostname = null;
    62→ *     @JsonProperty @Min(1025) public int port = 8080;
    63→ *   }
    64→ * </pre>
    65→ *
    66→ * And your Properties object had in it
    67→ *
    68→ * <pre>
    69→ *   druid.server.hostname=0.0.0.0
    70→ *   druid.server.port=3333
    71→ * </pre>
    72→ *
    73→ * Then this would bind a singleton instance of a DruidServerConfig object with hostname = "0.0.0.0" and port = 3333.
    74→ *
    75→ * If the port weren't set in the properties, then the default of 8080 would be taken.  Essentially, it is the same as
    76→ * subtracting the "druid.server" prefix from the properties and building a Map which is then passed into
    77→ * ObjectMapper.convertValue()
    78→ *
    79→ * @param <T> type of config object to provide.
    80→ */
    81→@PublicApi
    82→public class JsonConfigProvider<T> implements Provider<Supplier<T>>
    83→{
    84→  @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    85→  public static <T> void bind(Binder binder, String propertyBase, Class<T> classToProvide)
    86→  {
    87→    bind(
    88→        binder,
    89→        propertyBase,
    90→        classToProvide,
    91→        Key.get(classToProvide),
    92→        (Key) Key.get(Types.newParameterizedType(Supplier.class, classToProvide))
    93→    );
    94→  }
